Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below is a quick mapping of the columns that matter for the requested analysis together with the main filter conditions, followed by ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (simple → complex) that gradually build understanding and finish with the side‑by‑side length comparison.  
Every column name is wrapped in double quotes and each query is limited to 20 rows to stay light.

Relevant columns & potential use  
• "CLASS": main road class → GROUP BY / display  
• "SUBCLASS": finer road class → GROUP BY / display  
• "LENGTH_M": text field holding the road length in meters → needs TRY_TO_DOUBLE() cast, then SUM()  
• "QUADKEY": Bing‑quadkey tile id → use as city filter  
    – Amsterdam filter: "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020210%'  
    – Rotterdam filter: "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020211%'  

(Other columns such as "ID", "GEO_CORDINATES", "NAMES" are not required for the requested metric.)

SQL‑snippets
```sql
-- 1) Description: Peek at a few rows from V_ROAD to verify basic content
SELECT *
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
LIMIT 20;

-- 2) Description: Distinct road classes present in entire dataset
SELECT DISTINCT "CLASS"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
LIMIT 20;

-- 3) Description: Distinct subclasses within each class (Amsterdam quadkey only)
SELECT DISTINCT "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020210%'
LIMIT 20;

-- 4) Description: How many road segments per class / subclass in Amsterdam
SELECT "CLASS",
       "SUBCLASS",
       COUNT(*) AS "segment_cnt"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020210%'
GROUP BY "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
ORDER BY "segment_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 5) Description: Same segment counts for Rotterdam
SELECT "CLASS",
       "SUBCLASS",
       COUNT(*) AS "segment_cnt"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020211%'
GROUP BY "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
ORDER BY "segment_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 6) Description: Distribution of LENGTH_M values (Amsterdam) to inspect text‑to‑numeric conversion
SELECT "LENGTH_M"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020210%'
  AND "LENGTH_M" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;

-- 7) Description: Total road length (meters) per class/subclass for Amsterdam
SELECT "CLASS",
       "SUBCLASS",
       SUM(TRY_TO_DOUBLE("LENGTH_M")) AS "amsterdam_len_m"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020210%'
GROUP BY "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
ORDER BY "amsterdam_len_m" DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 8) Description: Same total lengths for Rotterdam
SELECT "CLASS",
       "SUBCLASS",
       SUM(TRY_TO_DOUBLE("LENGTH_M")) AS "rotterdam_len_m"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020211%'
GROUP BY "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
ORDER BY "rotterdam_len_m" DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 9) Description: Combine both cities using UNION ALL so we can quickly eyeball combined data
SELECT 'Amsterdam' AS "city",
       "CLASS",
       "SUBCLASS",
       SUM(TRY_TO_DOUBLE("LENGTH_M")) AS "total_len_m"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020210%'
GROUP BY "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
UNION ALL
SELECT 'Rotterdam' AS "city",
       "CLASS",
       "SUBCLASS",
       SUM(TRY_TO_DOUBLE("LENGTH_M")) AS "total_len_m"
FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020211%'
GROUP BY "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
LIMIT 20;

-- 10) Description: Final side‑by‑side comparison of total road length (meters)
SELECT
    COALESCE(a."CLASS", r."CLASS")        AS "class",
    COALESCE(a."SUBCLASS", r."SUBCLASS")  AS "subclass",
    a."amsterdam_len_m",
    r."rotterdam_len_m"
FROM
    ( SELECT "CLASS",
             "SUBCLASS",
             SUM(TRY_TO_DOUBLE("LENGTH_M")) AS "amsterdam_len_m"
      FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
      WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020210%'
      GROUP BY "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
    ) AS a
FULL OUTER JOIN
    ( SELECT "CLASS",
             "SUBCLASS",
             SUM(TRY_TO_DOUBLE("LENGTH_M")) AS "rotterdam_len_m"
      FROM "NETHERLANDS_OPEN_MAP_DATA"."NETHERLANDS"."V_ROAD"
      WHERE "QUADKEY" LIKE '12020211%'
      GROUP BY "CLASS", "SUBCLASS"
    ) AS r
  ON a."CLASS" = r."CLASS"
 AND a."SUBCLASS" = r."SUBCLASS"
LIMIT 20;
```
